+## Bot traffic filtering + admin Insights (2026-10-01, branch `feature/admin-insights-and-bot-filter`)
+
+**Why.** Read-only diagnosis of prod on 2026-10-01 found **44% of all `Visit` rows were bots** that the
+old coarse `BOT_RE` in `/api/track` let through: `Lightpanda/1.0` (a headless browser that executes
+JS and fires the beacon — 17,147 rows in 7 days from 16,183 residential-proxy IPs; 596k requests /
+18k IPs in the access log) and a stale-UA fleet (Chrome 118-121 / Firefox 120-121 rotated across
+~400 IPs, one page each, 25-26 Sep). Declared crawlers (Googlebot, Amazonbot — 23.6k requests on
+2026-09-30 vs Googlebot's 321 — Bingbot, ClaudeBot, GPTBot, …) never reached `Visit` at all because
+they were dropped, so there was no way to see what they were doing to the ~65k static pages.
+
+**Classification** — one pure function, `lib/bots/classify.ts` `classifyHit()`, used by ingest, the
+worker, the backfill and the log parser:
+
+| Kind | Rule |
+|---|---|
+| `verified-crawler` | catalogue UA (`lib/bots/catalogue.ts`, ~70 named bots) AND the IP is in the crawler's official published IP list (Google, Bing, Apple, OpenAI ×3 — committed in `lib/bots/datacenter-ranges.json`) or passes forward-confirmed reverse DNS (`lib/bots/verify.ts`, cached 14d in `CrawlerIpVerdict`) |
+| `declared-crawler` | self-declared bot we can't (or haven't yet) verified; long-tail `bot/crawl/spider/+http` UAs |
+| `scraper` | headless/automation/HTTP-library UA (Lightpanda, HeadlessChrome, python-requests, curl, Go, bare `node`, …), empty UA, a verifiable crawler UA that FAILS FCrDNS (spoof), honeypot/velocity/session-sweep evidence |
+| `suspected-bot` | browser-looking UA scoring ≥3 on weak signals: stale browser build (≥24 majors behind, estimated from the release cadence — never a hard-coded version), iOS ≤13, non-browser/truncated UA, datacenter IP (21 providers, 12.6k v4 + 4.5k v6 merged ranges from AWS/GCP/Oracle feeds + RIPEstat ASN prefixes; Cloudflare/WARP deliberately excluded), `navigator.webdriver`, or a UA cluster (≥25 IPs/day, ≥90% referrer-less single-page landings) |
+| `human` | none of the above. A **signed-in** account is never flagged on weak signals alone. |
+
+Columns added to `Visit` (additive, nullable/defaulted): `isBot` (default false), `botKind`,
+`botReason`, `botCheckedAt`, `interacted`, `webdriver`; index `(isBot, createdAt)`. New models:
+`BotIpFlag` (expiring honeypot/velocity flags), `CrawlerIpVerdict`, `CrawlerDaily`, `CrawlerUrl`,
+`CrawlLogCursor`, `InsightsSnapshot`, `InsightsAlert`.
+
+- **Ingest** (`app/api/track/route.ts`): bots are now STORED and labelled instead of dropped (only an
+  empty UA is skipped); declared crawlers are capped at 300 rows/min each. `components/VisitTracker.tsx`
+  sends `wd` (webdriver) on the pageview and `ix` (any real pointer/scroll/key/touch) on the close
+  beacon, and renders an invisible nofollow honeypot link to `/api/track/hp` (robots-disallowed under
+  `/api`); a hit there flags the IP for 7 days (never a signed-in account, never a declared crawler).
+- **Async** (`worker/bot-classify.ts`, every 5 min): velocity (>100 anonymous pageviews/10 min/IP),
+  session sweeps (≥25 pages, ~no dwell, no interaction), UA clusters, FCrDNS verification (20
+  lookups/sweep). Only ever upgrades a verdict.
+- **Every analytics read excludes bots**: `lib/analytics.ts` `ipEx()` (now exported as `visitScope`)
+  adds `isBot: false`; also `lib/retention.ts` (win-back/retention), `lib/user-attribution.ts`
+  (acquisition source), `lib/google-ads.ts` (offline conversion upload — a bot hit can never become a
+  conversion), `components/admin/GoogleAdsClicksPanel.tsx`. `VisitorDaily` rollups are always bot-free.
+  **Admin "include bots" toggle**: per-browser cookie `nx_inc_bots` (12h, `lib/actions-insights.ts`
+  `setIncludeBots`, audited) lifts only the bot filter on live views.
+- **Crawler activity** (`worker/crawler-log.ts`, every 2 min): incremental byte-offset parse of the
+  nginx access log (≤8 MB/tick, complete lines only, logrotate-safe via inode) into `CrawlerDaily`
+  (day × bot × kind × status class × section) and `CrawlerUrl` (per-URL last status/first/last seen).
+
+**Owner actions (not run by the agent — prod writes):**
+1. Deploy (db push adds the columns/tables — all additive).
+2. Backfill existing visits (idempotent, keyset batches of 2000, resumable, re-rolls VisitorDaily):
+   `cd /opt/nxeon && npx tsx scripts/backfill-bot-classification.ts --dry-run` then without `--dry-run`.
+   Expected on today's data: ~21k of 48k rows → bot (17.3k Lightpanda scraper, ~4.1k stale-browser).
+3. Optional crawler history from the rotated logs (idempotent by inode):
+   `cd /opt/nxeon && npx tsx scripts/backfill-crawler-log.ts --dry-run` then without.
+4. Quarterly: `npx tsx scripts/refresh-datacenter-ranges.ts` and commit `lib/bots/datacenter-ranges.json`.
+
+**`/admin/insights`** (`app/admin/insights/**`, `lib/insights/**`, area `analytics`, one nav entry in
+`lib/admin-groups.ts`): tabs Overview · Revenue · Churn & LTV · Funnel · Products & margin · Capacity
+· Jobs & support · Partners & email · Payments & refunds · Bots & crawlers. Date range (`?preset=` or
+`?from=&to=`, UTC) with compare-to-previous-period on every KPI; CSV export per tab
+(`/admin/insights/export`, audited `insights.export`). Definitions reuse the console's audited ones
+(`REVENUE_WHERE`, `REAL_CASH_IN_WHERE`, `fleetMrrCents`/`serverMonthlyCents`). Honest gaps shown on
+the page: MRR history only from the first `InsightsSnapshot` (worker writes daily); job queue-wait vs
+run-time needs `Job.startedAt/finishedAt` (auto-detected when D1 adds them; until then end-to-end
+only); chargebacks are admin-recorded only (no dispute webhook); email opens are MPP-inflated;
+margins are "cost incomplete" for any node without `monthlyCostCents`. Beyond-scope features ranked in
+`docs/ADMIN-INSIGHTS-PROPOSALS.md`; the top three are implemented — **low-capacity forecast alerts**,
+**revenue/payment anomaly alerts** (both hourly → `InsightsAlert`, page-only, no email) and the
+**churn-risk list**.
+
+**Verification:** `test/bot-classify.test.ts` (real UA fixtures incl. strings from our own log),
+`test/insights-stats.test.ts`; classifier evaluated read-only against prod UA aggregates and one day
+of the nginx log; backfill (dry-run, real, idempotent re-run), worker sweeps and logrotate handling
+exercised on a throwaway DB seeded by `scripts/seed-insights-sandbox.ts` (refuses non-scratch DBs);
+EXPLAIN ANALYZE at 300k synthetic rows: all Visit reads < 220 ms, velocity query uses the new index.
+
